<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · infrastructure</p><h1 class="enc-title">Band-e Kaisar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Band-e Kaisar was a combined bridge and dam on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karun-river">Karun River</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shushtar">Shushtar</a> in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, built under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> in the third century. Tradition holds that it was built with the labour of Roman prisoners captured by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shapur-i">Shapur I</a>. It was part of an irrigation system that supported agriculture in the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/band-e-kaisar.jpg" alt="Band-e Kaisar" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ali Afghah · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sushtar_Bridge.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
